# THE SIFREI ROWS OF PISKAOT 271-277 (THE DEUTERONOMY WALK sitting 17 — CHAPTERS 22-25, LEAN, RUN 2, 2026-09-26): the new wife — new to him, the year free of
# the host but not of supply, the four words (271); the mill and the upper stone, two vessels one work (272); the kidnapper — witnesses, no minor, his own son,
# the domain and the use, strangling, not the slave, the purge formula's last seat (273); the plague — a prohibition, the white hair, the quick flesh, garments
# and houses, the quarantine, the priests' minority (274); Miriam and slander (275); the loan — the wage and the credit, stand outside, the court's agent (276);
# the poor man's pledge — the rich too, no lying down with it, the day vessel and the night vessel, the blessing and the merit (277). Every row READ WHOLE in
# both files; the cuts by ch22_ink.SP_. Sitting 16's form.
from ch22_ink import *
S = {}
def srow(p, r, verdict, prose): S[(p, r)] = (verdict, prose)

srow(271, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"WHEN A MAN TAKES A NEW WIFE" (24:5) — ONLY A VIRGIN? A WIDOW AND ONE AWAITING THE LEVIR WHENCE? "REJOICE HIS WIFE" — ANY; WHY "NEW"? NEW TO HIM — EXCLUDING ONE WHO TAKES BACK HIS DIVORCEE, A WIDOW TO A HIGH PRIEST, A DIVORCEE OR RELEASED WIDOW TO A COMMON PRIEST, A MAMZERET OR NETINAH TO AN ISRAELITE, AN ISRAELITE\'S DAUGHTER TO A MAMZER OR NATIN. The head row of piska 271 ({SP_(271, 1, "לרבות", "אלמנה", "ושומרת", "יבם")} "to include a widow and one awaiting the levir"; {SP_(271, 1, "מי", "שחדשה", "לו")} "one who is new to him"; {SP_(271, 1, "פרט", "למחזיר", "גרושתו")} "excluding one who takes back his divorcee"; {SP_(271, 1, "ואלמנה", "לכהן", "גדול")} "a widow to a high priest"): THE FORBIDDEN MARRIAGES EXCLUDED FROM THE YEAR — Leviticus 21\'s priestly bars and 23:3\'s mamzer the callees; Sotah 8:4\'s kin (the design\'s DV24-02). Fresh.')
srow(271, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'"HE SHALL NOT GO OUT IN THE HOST" — BUT SUPPLY WEAPONS, WATER AND FOOD? "NOR SHALL ANY MATTER PASS UPON HIM"; THEN EVEN HE WHO BUILT A HOUSE AND DID NOT DEDICATE IT, PLANTED A VINEYARD, BETROTHED A WOMAN? "UPON HIM" — UPON HIM IT DOES NOT PASS, UPON ALL THESE IT PASSES. ({SP_(271, 2, "אבל", "יספק", "כלי", "זין", "ומים", "ומזון")} "but supplies weapons, water and food"; {SP_(271, 2, "בנה", "בית", "ולא", "חנכו")} "built a house and did not dedicate it"; {SP_(271, 2, "עליו", "אינו", "עובר")} "upon him it does not pass"): 20:5-7\'S THREE RETURN HOME BUT SERVE SUPPLY (16b\'s war cells — Sotah 8:2\'s parameter), THE NEWLYWED FREE OF ALL — the exemption widened (the design\'s (b)); the Tosefta\'s row. Fresh.')
srow(271, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'"FREE SHALL HE BE FOR HIS HOUSE" — THIS IS HIS HOUSE. ({SP_(271, 3, "זה", "ביתו")} "this is his house"): the first of four words each a class. Fresh.')
srow(271, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'"SHALL HE BE" — THIS IS HIS VINEYARD. ({SP_(271, 4, "זה", "כרמו")} "this is his vineyard"): the second. Fresh.')
srow(271, 5, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND REJOICE HIS WIFE" — THIS IS HIS WIFE. ({SP_(271, 5, "זו", "אשתו")} "this is his wife"): the third — the year for the house, the vineyard and the wife of 20:5-7 gathered. Fresh.')
srow(271, 6, 'MATERIAL', f'"WHOM HE TOOK" — TO INCLUDE HIS LEVIRATE WIDOW. ({SP_(271, 6, "להביא", "את", "יבמתו")} "to include his levirate widow"): the fourth — 25:5\'s widow in the year; the parser\'s [1] "one year" the CLOCK parameter (Sotah 8:4). Fresh.')
srow(272, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"HE SHALL NOT TAKE IN PLEDGE THE MILL AND THE UPPER STONE" (24:6) — ONLY THESE? ANYTHING WHENCE? "FOR HE TAKES A LIFE IN PLEDGE"; WHY THESE? AS THEY ARE TWO VESSELS SERVING ONE WORK AND HE IS LIABLE FOR EACH BY ITSELF, SO ANY TWO VESSELS SERVING ONE WORK. The head row of piska 272 ({SP_(272, 1, "מנין", "לרבות", "כל", "דבר")} "whence to include everything?"; {SP_(272, 1, "שני", "כלים", "ומשמשים", "מלאכה", "אחת")} "two vessels serving one work"; {SP_(272, 1, "וחיב", "על", "זה", "בפני", "עצמו")} "liable for this one by itself"): THE LIVELIHOOD\'S TOOLS the class, the two stones the prototype counted twice — Bava Metzia 9:13 the compile\'s answer sheet (the design\'s DV24-02); the verse with no kin (find 12). Fresh.')
srow(272, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'"FOR HE TAKES A LIFE IN PLEDGE" — TO TELL WHAT CAUSED IT. ({SP_(272, 2, "להגיד", "מה", "גרם")} "to tell what caused it"): the reason clause named as a reason — the livelihood the life; Onkelos paraphrases "with them food is made for every soul" (24:6\'s row). Fresh.')
srow(273, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"IF A MAN BE FOUND" (24:7) — BY WITNESSES. The head row of piska 273 ({SP_(273, 1, "בעדים")} "by witnesses"): the court\'s condition — 19:15\'s two witnesses the callee. Fresh.')
srow(273, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'"A MAN" — EXCLUDING A MINOR. ({SP_(273, 2, "פרט", "לקטן")} "excluding a minor"): the thief\'s age parameter (255:2\'s form). Fresh.')
srow(273, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'"STEALING A SOUL OF HIS BROTHERS" — AND NOT OF OTHERS. ({SP_(273, 3, "ולא", "מאחרים")} "and not of others"): the victim an Israelite. Fresh.')
srow(273, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'"OF THE CHILDREN OF ISRAEL" — TO INCLUDE ONE WHO STEALS HIS OWN SON AND SELLS HIM, LIABLE: R. YOHANAN B. BEROKA; THE SAGES: EXEMPT. ({SP_(273, 4, "להביא", "הגונב", "את", "בנו", "ומוכרו")} "to include one who steals his own son and sells him"; {SP_(273, 4, "פטור")} "exempt"): the father\'s case disputed — Exodus 21:16\'s cell (the design\'s (e)), the Mekhilta\'s row the English names. Fresh.')
srow(273, 5, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND ENSLAVES HIM" — NOT LIABLE UNTIL HE BRINGS HIM INTO HIS DOMAIN; R. JUDAH: UNTIL HE BRINGS HIM IN AND USES HIM — "ENSLAVES HIM AND SELLS HIM". ({SP_(273, 5, "עד", "שיכניסנו", "לרשותו")} "until he brings him into his domain"; {SP_(273, 5, "וישתמש", "בו")} "and uses him"): Sanhedrin 11:1\'s row (the English\'s "//") — the domain and the use two conditions, the second disputed. Fresh.')
srow(273, 6, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND THAT THIEF SHALL DIE" — AN UNSPECIFIED DEATH IN THE TORAH IS STRANGLING. ({SP_(273, 6, "בסתם", "מיתה", "האמורה", "בתורה", "בחנק")} "an unspecified death in the Torah is strangling"): THE DEATH\'S MODE by the default rule (155:1\'s, the English) — the sanction\'s parameter. Fresh.')
srow(273, 7, 'MATERIAL', f'"THAT" — AND NOT ONE WHO STEALS A SLAVE. ({SP_(273, 7, "ולא", "הגונב", "את", "העבד")} "not one who steals a slave"): the victim\'s class narrowed. Fresh.')
srow(273, 8, 'MATERIAL', f'"THAT" — AND NOT ONE WHO STEALS ONE HALF SLAVE AND HALF FREE. ({SP_(273, 8, "שחציו", "עבד", "וחציו", "בן", "חורים")} "half slave and half free"): the mixed status excluded (Sanhedrin 11:1 the English\'s "cf."). Fresh.')
srow(273, 9, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND YOU SHALL PURGE THE EVIL FROM YOUR MIDST" — PURGE THE DOERS OF EVIL FROM ISRAEL. ({SP_(273, 9, "בער", "עושי", "הרעות", "מישראל")} "purge the doers of evil from Israel"): THE PURGE FORMULA\'S NINTH AND LAST SEAT (find 6; 13:6 the first) — the effect the same at every seat (the English\'s list of its piskaot); Onkelos "the doer of evil" (24:7\'s row). Fresh.')
srow(274, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"TAKE HEED" (24:8) — A NEGATIVE COMMANDMENT. The head row of piska 274 ({SP_(274, 1, "בלא", "תעשה")} "under a negative commandment"): the chapter\'s one imperative (find 14) read as a prohibition — the book\'s "take heed" (4:9). Fresh.')
srow(274, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'"IN THE PLAGUE" — THIS IS THE WHITE HAIR. ({SP_(274, 2, "זה", "שער", "לבן")} "this is white hair"): Leviticus 13:3\'s sign the first — the daemon\'s parameters cited by name (the design\'s DV24-03). Fresh.')
srow(274, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'"OF LEPROSY" — THIS IS THE QUICK FLESH; ONLY BEFORE HE IS BOUND TO UNCLEANNESS? ONCE BOUND, AND AFTER THE RELEASE WHENCE? "TO KEEP DILIGENTLY AND TO DO". ({SP_(274, 3, "זו", "מחיה")} "this is quick flesh"; {SP_(274, 3, "משנזקק", "לטמאה")} "once bound to uncleanness"; {SP_(274, 3, "ואחר", "הפטור", "מנין")} "and after the release — whence?"): the second sign (Leviticus 13:10) and the bar on cutting a sign through the plague\'s three states — before, during, after. Fresh.')
srow(274, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'ONLY PLAGUES OF MEN? OF GARMENTS AND OF HOUSES WHENCE? "AS THE LEVITICAL PRIESTS TEACH YOU". ({SP_(274, 4, "נגעי", "בגדים", "ונגעי", "בתים", "מנין")} "plagues of garments and of houses — whence?"): Leviticus 13:47 and 14:34\'s two other subjects — the daemon\'s three ranges. Fresh.')
srow(274, 5, 'MATERIAL', f'ONLY FROM THE CONFIRMED? FROM THE QUARANTINE WHENCE? "AS I COMMANDED THEM". ({SP_(274, 5, "מתוך", "החלט")} "from the confirmed"; {SP_(274, 5, "מתוך", "הסגר", "מנין")} "from the quarantine — whence?"): the two states of the leper (confirmed, shut up) — Onkelos names the plague by the quarantine (24:8\'s row). Fresh.')
srow(274, 6, 'MATERIAL', f'ONLY ALL OF THEM? EVEN SOME OF THE PRIESTS WHENCE? "TO KEEP"; "AND TO DO" — YOU GO ON DOING AND NEED NOT FEAR LEST HIS LEPROSY WENT AWAY. ({SP_(274, 6, "מנין", "אף", "מקצתם")} "whence even some of them?"; {SP_(274, 6, "ואי", "אתה", "חושש")} "and you need not fear"; {SP_(274, 6, "שמא", "הלכה", "לה", "צרעתו")} "lest his leprosy went away"): a minority of priests decides; the sign that falls off in the course of work no offense (the Tosefta\'s row). Fresh.')
srow(275, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"REMEMBER WHAT THE LORD YOUR GOD DID TO MIRIAM" (24:9) — WHAT HAS THIS TO DO WITH THAT? PLAGUES COME ONLY FOR SLANDER; AN A FORTIORI: MIRIAM SPOKE OUT OF MOSES\' HEARING, FOR HIS GOOD, IN THE OMNIPRESENT\'S PRAISE, FOR THE WORLD\'S BUILDING — AND WAS PUNISHED; ONE WHO SPEAKS HIS FELLOW\'S SHAME IN PUBLIC ALL THE MORE. The head row of piska 275 ({SP_(275, 1, "מה", "ענין", "זה", "לזה")} "what has this to do with that?"; {SP_(275, 1, "שאין", "נגעים", "באים", "אלא", "על", "לשון", "הרע")} "plagues come only for slander"; {SP_(275, 1, "קל", "וחמר")} "an a fortiori argument"): THE ADJACENCY READ AS A CAUSE — Numbers 12 the tape\'s own line (the RUN CITATION behind, the design\'s readback); the second "remember" (find 2). Fresh.')
srow(275, 2, 'CONTEXT', f'"ON THE WAY" — IN THE HOUR OF YOUR CONFUSION. ({SP_(275, 2, "בשעת", "טרופכם")} "in the hour of your confusion"): 250:2\'s gloss repeated for the phrase\'s second seat. Fresh.')
srow(275, 3, 'CONTEXT', f'"WHEN YOU CAME OUT OF EGYPT" — IN THE HOUR OF YOUR REDEMPTION; SCRIPTURE HUNG IT ON MIRIAM TO TEACH THAT WHEN THE BANNERS JOURNEYED THEY WENT NOT UNTIL MIRIAM WENT BEFORE THEM — MICAH 6:4 "I SENT BEFORE YOU MOSES, AARON AND MIRIAM". ({SP_(275, 3, "בשעת", "גאלתכם")} "in the hour of your redemption"; {SP_(275, 3, "שהיו", "הדגלים", "נוסעים")} "when the banners journeyed"; {SP_(275, 3, "עד", "שמרים", "מקדמת", "לפניהם")} "until Miriam went before them"): the seven days the camp waited (Numbers 12:15, on the tape) read as Miriam\'s precedence; Micah the receipt (250:1\'s twin verse). Fresh.')
srow(276, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"WHEN YOU LEND YOUR FELLOW" (24:10) — ONLY A LOAN? A HIRELING\'S WAGE AND SHOP CREDIT WHENCE? "A LOAN OF ANYTHING". The head row of piska 276 ({SP_(276, 1, "אין", "לי", "אלא", "מלוה")} "only a loan"; {SP_(276, 1, "לרבות", "שכר", "שכיר", "והקפת", "חנות")} "to include a hireling\'s wage and shop credit"): the debt\'s class widened — the pledge cell (Exodus 22:24-26, the design\'s (a)) with every debt as its trigger. Fresh.')
srow(276, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'"COME NOT INTO HIS HOUSE" — NOT FROM INSIDE BUT FROM OUTSIDE? "OUTSIDE YOU SHALL STAND" (24:11); NOT FROM OUTSIDE BUT FROM INSIDE? "OUTSIDE YOU SHALL STAND". ({SP_(276, 2, "לא", "ימשכננו", "מבפנים")} "he shall not take his pledge from inside"; {SP_(276, 2, "אבל", "ימשכננו", "מבחוץ")} "but takes it from outside"): the creditor takes nothing himself — Bava Metzia 9:13 (the English\'s "cf."). Fresh.')
srow(276, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'WHEN IT SAYS "AND THE MAN" — TO INCLUDE THE COURT\'S AGENT. ({SP_(276, 3, "לרבות", "שליח", "בית", "דין")} "to include the court\'s agent"): the one who may enter — the court\'s arm in the loan; 24:11 carries no head. Fresh.')
srow(277, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND IF HE IS A POOR MAN" (24:12) — ONLY THE POOR? THE RICH WHENCE? "IF A MAN"; WHY "POOR"? I HASTEN TO EXACT FOR THE POOR MORE THAN FOR THE RICH. The head row of piska 277 ({SP_(277, 1, "עשיר", "מנין")} "the rich — whence?"; {SP_(277, 1, "ממהר", "אני", "לפרע", "על", "ידי", "עני")} "I hasten to exact for the poor"): the rule for all, the poor named for the sanction\'s speed — the trope of 278:2 and 279:4. Fresh.')
srow(277, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'"LIE NOT DOWN IN HIS PLEDGE" — WOULD YOU THINK HE LIES IN IT? RATHER, LIE NOT DOWN WITH HIS PLEDGE BY YOU. ({SP_(277, 2, "שלא", "תשכב", "ועבוטו", "אצלך")} "that you not lie down with his pledge by you"): the night the bound — the pledge back before sleep. Fresh.')
srow(277, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'"SURELY RETURN HIM THE PLEDGE" (24:13) — A DAY VESSEL BY DAY AND A NIGHT VESSEL BY NIGHT: A BLANKET AT NIGHT AND A PLOW BY DAY, NOT THE REVERSE. ({SP_(277, 3, "כלי", "יום", "ביום", "וכלי", "לילה", "בלילה")} "a day vessel by day and a night vessel by night"; {SP_(277, 3, "סגוס", "בלילה", "ומחרשה", "ביום")} "a blanket by night and a plow by day"): THE CLOCK OF THE PLEDGE — two returns a day by the vessel\'s use (Bava Metzia 9:13\'s row); the sunset of 24:13 the night vessel\'s hour; 24:13 carries no head. Fresh.')
srow(277, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND HE LIES IN HIS GARMENT AND BLESSES YOU" — HE IS COMMANDED TO BLESS YOU; IF HE BLESSES YOU ARE BLESSED, IF NOT NOT? "AND IT SHALL BE RIGHTEOUSNESS TO YOU" — OF YOURSELF YOU DO RIGHTEOUSNESS. ({SP_(277, 4, "שהוא", "מצוה", "לברכך")} "that he is commanded to bless you"; {SP_(277, 4, "מעצמך", "אתה", "עושה", "צדקה")} "of yourself you do righteousness"): the debtor\'s blessing a duty, the creditor\'s merit independent of it — Onkelos "merit" (zekhuta, 24:13\'s row). Fresh.')
srow(277, 5, 'CONTEXT', f'"AND IT SHALL BE RIGHTEOUSNESS TO YOU" — RIGHTEOUSNESS ASCENDS BEFORE THE THRONE OF GLORY; PSALM 85:14 "RIGHTEOUSNESS GOES BEFORE HIM". ({SP_(277, 5, "שהצדקה", "עולה", "לפני", "כסא", "הכבוד")} "righteousness ascends before the throne of glory"): the Writings\' verse for the heaven entry — a homily on the reward. Fresh.')
